00000003,"pitch":-88,"move":"flight"}],"pacing":[{"t":"2026-11-21T00:00:00Z","speed":1}],"beats":[{"t":"2026-11-21T00:00:00Z","text":"Saudi-led coalition downs Houthi missiles, Al Jazeera reports.","cites":["news:aljazeera:ea106474e483"]},{"t":"2026-11-21T00:00:08Z","text":"The Wall Street Journal reported in October 2026 that Houthis have relied on Chinese equipment and parts to build a version of the Kheibar Shekan ballistic missile.","cites":["wiki:rev:1386755859:292"]},{"t":"2026-11-21T00:00:16Z","text":"The Houthis, officially known as Ansar Allah or Ansarullah, are a Zaydi revivalist and Shia Islamist political and paramilitary organization that emerged from Yemen in the 1990s.","cites":["wiki:rev:1386755859:0"]},{"t":"2026-11-21T00:00:24Z","text":"Houthis is headquartered in Saada, Yemen.","cites":["wd:Q3042087:P159"]},{"t":"2026-11-21T00:00:32Z","text":"Founded in 2000 by Hussein al-Houthi.","cites":["wd:Q3042087:P571","wd:Q3042087:P112"]},{"t":"2026-11-21T00:00:42Z","text":"19 November: The Houthis fire missiles at King Abdullah Financial District in Riyadh, Saudi Arabia, which damage the Public Investment Fund Tower and other buildings but cause no injuries.","cites":["wiki:2026-11-19:4"]},{"t":"2026-11-21T00:00:50Z","text":"20 November: The Saudi-led coalition launches airstrikes on Hodeidah, Yemen, targeting weapons smuggling used by the Houthis, and on targets in the Sanaa, Saada, and Taiz governorates.","cites":["wiki:2026-11-20:2"]},{"t":"2026-11-21T00:00:58Z","text":"20 November: Saudi coalition and Houthis exchange threats to bomb key ports, Al Jazeera reported.","cites":["news:aljazeera:4ce3712d8425"]},{"t":"2026-11-21T00:01:17Z","text":"Al Jazeera headlined it: “Iran war live: Saudi-led coalition downs Houthi missiles”","cites":["news:aljazeera:ea106474e483"]},{"t":"2026-11-21T00:01:25Z","text":"France 24 headlined it: “Houthis launch strikes on Saudi Arabia”","cites":["news:france24:258e24a13d6a"]},{"t":"2026-11-21T00:01:33Z","text":"Sources: 2 o